[[File:PrestigeOffer.jpg|thumb|275px|The Prestige Offer]]
'''Prestige''' is a feature in [[Murder Mystery 2]] that is only achievable after reaching level one hundred, with the purpose of resetting a player's normal level. If the player has accepted the prestige offer, their level will reset back to 1 and the number of times the player has prestiged will show left of their level in roman numerals on the leaderboard. The maximum amount of times a player can reset their level is ten times, making Prestige X the highest available.[[File:Screenshot_(59).png|thumb|Prestige X and III shown alongside levels 100 and 23[[File:Old prestigemm2.png|thumb|The old prestige prompt and level 100 icon.]]]]
==Benefits of Prestige==
Prestige does not offer any gameplay abilities. In fact, it's more on the "aesthetic" side. The higher a player's prestige is, the higher they are on the player leaderboard on the left side. For example, a player with Prestige I and level 1, will appear higher than someone with no prestige and level 100. Players with the same prestige will be ranked according to level. Prestige also makes the player appear more skilled, as they have been playing for a longer time than many average players.

==Levels Reached Each Prestige==
Each prestige level can be recognized as adding 100 to the player's level, technically making the highest level possible 1100 (X 100).
